\viewkind4\uc1\pard\fi-180\li180\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. The King of love my Shepherd is,\cf0 
\par \pard\li180\sl190\slmult0 Whose goodness faileth never;
\par I nothing lack if I am His
\par And He is mine for ever.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-180\li180\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Where streams of living water flow
\par \pard\li180\sl190\slmult0 My ransomed soul He leadeth,
\par And where the verdant pastures grow
\par With food celestial feedeth.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3.  Perverse and foolish oft I strayed;
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 But yet in love He sought me,
\par And on his shoulder gently laid,
\par And home rejoicing brought me.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-180\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. In death's dark vale I fear no ill
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 With Thee, dear Lord, beside me;
\par Thy rod and staff my comfort still,
\par Thy Cross before to guide me.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li270\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. Thou spread'st a table in my sight;
\par \pard\li270\sl190\slmult0 Thy unction grace bestoweth;
\par And O what transport of delight
\par From Thy pure chalice floweth!
\par 
\par \pard\fi-270\li270\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par  6.  And so through all the length of days
\par \pard\li270\sl190\slmult0\qj Thy goodness faileth never;
\par Good Shepherd, may I sing Thy praise
\par Within Thy house for ever!
\par \pard\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\f2\fs14 
\par }

